  "correct": "A",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Integrate with the parameter fixed",
      "body": "<p>Expand <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. When integrating with respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, treat <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> as a constant.</p>",
      "recap": "Only the integration variable changes during an integral.",
      "pitfall": "The integral of the constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Integrate the three terms and evaluate between 0 and 1.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l20",
          "reminder": "Only the integration variable changes during an integral."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Change the optimisation variable",
      "body": "<p>After integration the expression is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. You now minimise this value over real <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Evaluate the integral before optimising its parameter.",
      "pitfall": "The minimum integrand at an individual <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> does not determine the minimum of the whole integral.",
      "pause": "Complete the square in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l05",
          "reminder": "Evaluate the integral before optimising its parameter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Prove and attain the lower bound",
      "body": "<p>Rewrite the quadratic as a square plus a constant. The square is nonnegative, but also check that its zero occurs at an allowed value of the parameter.</p>",
      "recap": "A minimum is a lower bound reached at an allowed input.",
      "pitfall": "Report the least integral value, not the parameter producing it.",
      "pause": "Calculate the remaining constant after completing the square, then verify that this lower bound is attained.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l03",
          "reminder": "A minimum is a lower bound reached at an allowed input."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Expanding and integrating in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p>Complete the square: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>. This is at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>, with equality at the permitted value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The minimum is <strong><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>: A.</strong></p>",
